Subject: [PATCH] mcp: hide tools that require non-session auth

Targets Microck/kagi-cli v0.20.1 (src/main.rs).

This deployment authenticates with a Kagi session token only. Remove MCP
tools that cannot work with a session token from the tool catalog so MCP
clients never discover them:
  - kagi_extract        (requires KAGI_API_KEY)
  - kagi_fastgpt        (requires KAGI_API_TOKEN)
  - kagi_enrich_web     (requires KAGI_API_TOKEN)
  - kagi_enrich_news    (requires KAGI_API_TOKEN)
  - kagi_summarize      (default path requires KAGI_API_TOKEN)

Because validate_mcp_tool_call() checks tools/call names against the same
catalog, the hidden tools are rejected as unknown, not just hidden from
tools/list. The draft server/discover instructions are trimmed to match.

--- a/src/main.rs
+++ b/src/main.rs
@@ -3475,7 +3475,7 @@ fn mcp_discover_result() -> Value {
                 "version": env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION")
             }
         },
-        "instructions": "Search Kagi web and news, extract and summarize pages, inspect Assistant threads, and inspect Kagi account or local CLI state. Prompting Assistant or changing account and local state requires --enable-mutating-tools.",
+        "instructions": "Search Kagi web and news, inspect Assistant threads, and inspect Kagi account or local CLI state. Prompting Assistant or changing account and local state requires --enable-mutating-tools.",
         "ttlMs": MCP_CACHE_TTL_MS,
         "cacheScope": "public"
     })
@@ -3883,6 +3883,20 @@ fn build_mcp_tool_definitions(enable_mutating_tools: bool) -> Vec<Value> {
         ]);
     }
 
+    // This deployment authenticates with a Kagi session token only. Tools that
+    // rely on a Kagi API key or the legacy API token cannot work here, so drop
+    // them from the catalog entirely and keep MCP clients unaware of them.
+    tools.retain(|tool| {
+        !matches!(
+            tool["name"].as_str().unwrap_or_default(),
+            "kagi_extract"
+                | "kagi_fastgpt"
+                | "kagi_enrich_web"
+                | "kagi_enrich_news"
+                | "kagi_summarize"
+        )
+    });
+
     tools.sort_by(|left, right| {
         left["name"]
             .as_str()
